From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PS3 Linux project <ps3@localhost>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:37:02 +0300
Subject: hwengine: mask the FPU exceptions at start (EInvalidOp on ppc64)

Debian's ppc64 build log: the lua engine tests (stuckcake.lua, gravity_get_set.lua) die with
EInvalidOp before any simulation step. FPC's PowerPC runtime leaves the invalid-operation trap on;
the game code expects IEEE results. SetExceptionMask from unit Math at the start of the main
program, for all six exceptions. The physics (hwFloat) is fixed point and unaffected.

diff --git a/hedgewars/hwengine.pas b/hedgewars/hwengine.pas
--- a/hedgewars/hwengine.pas
+++ b/hedgewars/hwengine.pas
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@ uses {$IFDEF IPHONEOS}cmem, {$ENDIF} SDLh, uMisc, uConsole, uGame, uConsts, uLan
      , uSound, uScript, uTeams, uStats, uIO, uLocale, uChat, uAI, uAIMisc, uAILandMarks, uLandTexture, uCollisions
      , SysUtils, uTypes, uVariables, uCommands, uUtils, uCaptions, uDebug, uCommandHandlers, uLandPainted
      , uPhysFSLayer, uCursor, uRandom, ArgParsers, uVisualGearsHandlers, uTextures, uRender
+     {$IFNDEF PAS2C}, Math{$ENDIF}
      {$IFDEF USE_VIDEO_RECORDING}, uVideoRec {$ENDIF}
      {$IFDEF USE_TOUCH_INTERFACE}, uTouch {$ENDIF}
      {$IFDEF ANDROID}, GLUnit{$ENDIF}
@@ -674,6 +675,12 @@ begin
 {$IFNDEF PAS2C}
     // Custom procedure for unhandled exceptions; ExceptProc is used by SysUtils module
     ExceptProc:= @catchUnhandledException;
+
+    // On ppc64 the FPU traps an invalid operation (a NaN, 0/0, a float out of range for an integer
+    // conversion) and FPC raises EInvalidOp: Debian's buildd lua tests died with it before the first
+    // game step. Mask all FPU exceptions so such operations give IEEE results (NaN, Inf) as they do
+    // on the x86 builds the game is developed on.
+    SetExceptionMask([exInvalidOp, exDenormalized, exZeroDivide, exOverflow, exUnderflow, exPrecision]);
 {$ENDIF}
 
     preInitEverything();
